# Data Tables Reference

This section only applies to scripts that use Memberstack Data Tables. It covers the HTML attribute system for wiring UI elements and the JavaScript API for CRUD operations.

---

## HTML Attribute System

A small set of attributes to wire list, detail, form, edit, limit, and chart UIs to any data table without custom code per screen. One attribute equals one concern.

### Three Kinds of Attributes

| Kind | Purpose | Example |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `data-ms-code` | Role -- identifies the element (container, template, loading, error, etc.). | `data-ms-code="list-container"` |
| `ms-code-*` | Config -- table name, field names, URLs, options. One attribute per setting. | `ms-code-table="my-table"` |
| `data-ms-field` + `ms-field` | Field binding -- which record field to show or edit, and how. | `data-ms-field="title"` `ms-field="text"` |

Scripts find elements by role and read config from the same element. No duplicate or overlapping config attributes.

### Configuration Attributes

Place these on the container that drives the behaviour (form, list wrapper, detail wrapper, chart wrapper).

| Attribute | Purpose | Example / Default |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `ms-code-table` | Which data table (collection) to use. | Any table name |
| `ms-code-owner-field` | Field that stores the current user's ID (for "my records" and permission). | Any field name |
| `ms-code-id-param` | URL query param that holds the record ID. | `id` (so `?id=abc123`) |
| `ms-code-detail-page` | Base URL for "view one record" links. | Any page path |
| `ms-code-redirect` | Where to send the user after create, update, or delete. | Any page path |
| `ms-code-filter-field` | (Lists) Filter by this field; value comes from URL param. | Any field name |
| `ms-code-sort` | (Lists) Sort order. | `field:asc` or `field:desc` |
| `ms-code-per-page` | (Lists) Rows per page. | `10` |
| `ms-code-linked-field` | (Create form) Field that stores a related record ID. | Any field name |
| `ms-code-prevent-duplicates` | (Create form) Block duplicate records (same user + same linked ID). | `true` |
| `ms-code-limit` | (Quota) Max number of records that count toward the limit. | Any number |
| `ms-code-limit-when` | (Quota) Only count records where a field has a specific value. | `field:value` |
| `ms-code-unlimited` | (Quota) Comma-separated plan/role IDs that skip the limit. | Plan IDs |
| `ms-code-chart-type` | (Chart) Kind of chart. | `bar`, `line`, `doughnut` |
| `ms-code-group` | (Chart) Field to group by, or `month`/`week` for time. | Any field name |
| `ms-code-date-field` | (Chart) Field used for time grouping. | Any date field |
| `ms-code-value-field` | (Chart) Sum this number instead of counting. | Any numeric field |
| `ms-code-join` | (Chart) Data via another table: `table:field`. | `table:field` |
| `ms-code-label-field` | (Chart) Show this field from the joined table as axis label. | Any field name |
| `ms-code-max-records` | (Chart) Max records to load. | `100` |

Rules: Use one attribute per setting. Reuse the same name everywhere (e.g. `ms-code-id-param` for detail, edit, and list filter). Use `ms-code-owner-field` both for "who owns this record" and "set current user on create".

### Element Roles (`data-ms-code`)

Scripts look for these values to find the right DOM nodes. One role per purpose.

| Role | Values |
| --- | --- |
| List | `list-container`, `list-template`, `list-loading`, `list-empty`, `list-error`, `list-pagination`, `list-prev`, `list-next`, `list-page-info`, `detail-link` |
| Detail | `detail-container`, `detail-loading`, `detail-error`, `detail-content`, `array-template` |
| Form (create) | `form`, `form-loading`, `form-success`, `form-error`, `limit-banner` |
| Edit | `edit-container`, `edit-loading`, `edit-error`, `edit-content`, `edit-not-owner`, `confirm-delete` |
| Chart | `analytics-chart`, `analytics-canvas`, `analytics-loading`, `analytics-error` |

State indicators: forms can receive `data-ms-code-limit-reached="true"` when a limit is hit. Charts can receive `data-ms-code-state="loading"`, `"error"`, or `"content"`. Style these in CSS.

### Field Binding and Behaviour

| Attribute | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `data-ms-field` | Record field name. Script sets or reads this field. |
| `ms-field` | How to handle it: `text`, `html`, `date`, `image`, `link`, `number`, `checkbox`, `array`. Default `text`. |
| `data-ms-show-if` | Show element only when this field equals `data-ms-show-value` (or is not empty if no value set). |
| `data-ms-hide-if` | Hide element when this field equals `data-ms-hide-value` (or is not empty). |
| `data-ms-hide-empty` | If `true`, hide when the bound field is empty. |
| `data-ms-action` | Element triggers an action: `submit`, `apply`, `delete`, `delete-yes`, `delete-no`, `status`. |
| `data-ms-record-id` | Holds a record ID (e.g. parent ID for a create form). |

For inline edit UIs, use `data-ms-edit` with the field name and optional `ms-edit-type` (`text`, `richtext`, `select`), `ms-edit-placeholder`, `ms-edit-required`.

### Use Cases (Minimal Setup)

| Use Case | Container Attributes | Element Roles |
| --- | --- | --- |
| List ("My records") | `ms-code-table`, `ms-code-owner-field`, `ms-code-detail-page`, optional: `ms-code-sort`, `ms-code-per-page` | list-container, list-template, list-loading, list-empty, list-error, list-pagination, detail-link |
| Filtered list (by URL param) | Same as list + `ms-code-filter-field` | Same as list |
| Detail (one record by ID) | `ms-code-table`, `ms-code-id-param`, optional: `ms-code-owner-field`, `ms-code-redirect` | detail-container, detail-loading, detail-error, detail-content |
| Create form | `ms-code-table`, `ms-code-owner-field`, optional: `ms-code-redirect`, `ms-code-linked-field`, `ms-code-prevent-duplicates` | form, form-loading, form-success, form-error |
| Quota limit | Same as form + `ms-code-limit`, `ms-code-limit-when`, `ms-code-unlimited` | Same as form + limit-banner |
| Edit (update/delete) | `ms-code-table`, `ms-code-id-param`, `ms-code-owner-field`, optional: `ms-code-redirect` | edit-container, edit-loading, edit-error, edit-content, edit-not-owner, confirm-delete |
| Chart | `ms-code-table`, `ms-code-chart-type`, `ms-code-group`, optional: `ms-code-owner-field`, `ms-code-date-field`, `ms-code-value-field`, `ms-code-join`, `ms-code-label-field`, `ms-code-max-records` | analytics-chart, analytics-canvas, analytics-loading, analytics-error |

### Attribute Quick Reference

- **Roles** (`data-ms-code`) = which block is this (container, template, loading, error, etc.).
- **Config** (`ms-code-*`) = one attribute per setting (table, owner field, ID param, detail page, redirect, filter, sort, limit, chart options).
- **Fields** (`data-ms-field`, `ms-field`) = bind a DOM element to a record field and define how to render or edit it.
- **Conditionals** (`data-ms-show-if`, `data-ms-hide-if`, `data-ms-hide-empty`) = show or hide by field value.
- **Actions** (`data-ms-action`, `data-ms-record-id`) = buttons and record context.

Keep one attribute per concern so the same names work across list, detail, form, edit, limit, and chart UIs with any data table backend.

