## JavaScript API

### Field Types

| Type | Usage | Example |
| --- | --- | --- |
| TEXT | Standard text fields. | `{ title: 'My Title' }` |
| NUMBER | Numeric values. | `{ count: 5 }` |
| MEMBER_REFERENCE | Links to a member. Use the member ID directly. | `{ owner: member.id }` |
| REFERENCE | Links to another record. Try direct ID, fall back to object. | `{ parent: recordId }` or `{ parent: { id: recordId } }` |
| DATE | ISO 8601 date strings. | `{ created_at: new Date().toISOString() }` |

### Creating Records

Use `createDataRecord` to add new records to a table.

```javascript
var result = await memberstack.createDataRecord({
  table: 'table_name',
  data: {
    field1: 'value1',
    field2: 'value2',
  },
});

var record = result.data;
var recordId = record.id;
```

### Handling REFERENCE Fields

REFERENCE fields link to other records. Try the direct ID first, then fall back to object format.

```javascript
try {
  result = await memberstack.createDataRecord({
    table: 'table_name',
    data: {
      parent_record: parentId,       // Direct ID (preferred)
      owner: member.id,              // MEMBER_REFERENCE uses direct ID
      content: 'Some content',
      created_at: new Date().toISOString(),
    },
  });
} catch (err) {
  result = await memberstack.createDataRecord({
    table: 'table_name',
    data: {
      parent_record: { id: parentId }, // Object format (fallback)
      owner: member.id,
      content: 'Some content',
      created_at: new Date().toISOString(),
    },
  });
}
```

### Updating Records

Use `updateDataRecord` to modify existing records. Only include fields you want to change.

```javascript
var result = await memberstack.updateDataRecord({
  recordId: 'record_id_here',
  data: {
    status: 'new_status',
    updated_at: new Date().toISOString(),
  },
});

var updatedRecord = result.data;
```

To clear a field, set it to `null`:

```javascript
await memberstack.updateDataRecord({
  recordId: recordId,
  data: {
    assigned_member: null,
    updated_at: new Date().toISOString(),
  },
});
```

### Querying Records

Use `queryDataRecords` for filtering, sorting, and pagination. Handle different response shapes: `result.data?.records || result.data || []`.

```javascript
var result = await memberstack.queryDataRecords({
  table: 'table_name',
  query: {
    where: {
      owner: { equals: member.id },
    },
    orderBy: { created_at: 'desc' },
    take: 100,
  },
});

if ('records' in (result.data || {})) {
  var records = (result.data).records || [];
}
```

### Complex Filtering

Build `where` clauses dynamically based on your needs.

```javascript
var where = {};

if (filterByOwner) {
  where.owner = { equals: member.id };
}
if (filterStatus) {
  where.status = { equals: filterStatus };
}
if (filterCategory) {
  where.category = { equals: filterCategory };
}

var query = {
  orderBy: { created_at: 'desc' },
  take: 100,
};

if (Object.keys(where).length > 0) {
  query.where = where;
}

var result = await memberstack.queryDataRecords({
  table: 'table_name',
  query: query,
});
```

### Getting a Single Record

Use `getDataRecord` to fetch one record by ID.

```javascript
var result = await memberstack.getDataRecord({
  recordId: 'record_id_here',
});

var record = result.data;
var fieldValues = record.data;
```

Or query by ID:

```javascript
var result = await memberstack.queryDataRecords({
  table: 'table_name',
  query: {
    where: { id: { equals: recordId } },
    take: 1,
  },
});

if ('records' in (result.data || {})) {
  var record = (result.data).records[0] || null;
}
```

### Pagination and Bulk Loading

When you need more than 100 records, paginate using `skip`. Memberstack limits `take` to 1-100.

```javascript
var PAGE_SIZE = 100;

async function fetchAllRecords(memberstack, table, where) {
  var all = [];
  var skip = 0;
  var page = [];

  do {
    var result = await memberstack.queryDataRecords({
      table: table,
      query: {
        where: where,
        take: PAGE_SIZE,
        skip: skip,
      },
    });

    page = (result.data)?.records || [];
    all.push.apply(all, page);
    skip += page.length;
  } while (page.length === PAGE_SIZE);

  return all;
}
```

Prefer a single bulk load over per-item queries:

```javascript
// Instead of querying once per UI element, load all records and map them
var records = await fetchAllRecords(memberstack, 'table_name', {
  owner: { equals: member.id },
});

var byRelatedId = {};
records.forEach(function(r) {
  var related = r.data?.related_field;
  var id = related && (related.id || related);
  if (id) byRelatedId[id] = r.id;
});
```

### Query Operators

| Operator | Description | Example |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `equals` | Exact match (also works with `null`). | `{ status: { equals: 'active' } }` |
| `notEquals` | Not equal. | `{ status: { notEquals: 'closed' } }` |
| `contains` | Text contains substring. | `{ title: { contains: 'search' } }` |
| `startsWith` | Text starts with value. | `{ title: { startsWith: 'A' } }` |
| `endsWith` | Text ends with value. | `{ title: { endsWith: 'Z' } }` |
| `greaterThan` | Greater than. | `{ count: { greaterThan: 5 } }` |
| `lessThan` | Less than. | `{ count: { lessThan: 10 } }` |
| `in` | Matches any value in array. | `{ status: { in: ['a', 'b'] } }` |
| `notIn` | Matches none of the values. | `{ status: { notIn: ['x'] } }` |

### Data Table Error Handling

For critical operations, throw on failure:

```javascript
try {
  var result = await memberstack.createDataRecord({
    table: 'table_name',
    data: recordData,
  });
  return result.data;
} catch (error) {
  throw new Error(error?.message || 'Failed to create record');
}
```

For non-critical operations (e.g. logging), catch silently and continue:

```javascript
try {
  await memberstack.createDataRecord({
    table: 'audit_log',
    data: logData,
  });
} catch (logError) {
  // Logging failed but main operation succeeded -- continue
}
```

For tables that may not exist yet, degrade gracefully:

```javascript
try {
  var result = await memberstack.queryDataRecords({
    table: 'table_name',
    query: { take: 100 },
  });
  return result.data?.records || [];
} catch (error) {
  if (error?.message?.includes('not found') ||
      error?.message?.includes('does not exist')) {
    return [];
  }
  return [];
}
```

### Common Issues and Solutions

**REFERENCE field not working:** Try both direct ID and object format. Direct ID is preferred; object format (`{ id: recordId }`) is the fallback.

**Query returns empty results:** Verify field names match exactly, check access rules, and ensure you wrap values in an operator. Use `{ field: { equals: value } }`, not `{ field: value }`.

**Cannot update record:** Verify update permissions and use `recordId` as a parameter, not inside the `data` object.

**MEMBER_REFERENCE field not linking:** Use the member ID directly (`member.id`), not wrapped in an object.